  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is constrained to move along with a moveable pulley of mass&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;which is connected to a spring of force constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi></math>,&nbsp;as shown in the figure. If the mass of the fixed pulley is negligible and friction is absent everywhere, then the period of small oscillations of the system is<br />\r<u><strong><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0014752_Ques1_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 203px; height: 257px;\" /></strong></u></p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
